config WDT_XEN
	bool "Xen domain watchdog driver"
	default y
	depends on XEN
	depends on DT_HAS_XEN_WATCHDOG_ENABLED
	select HAS_WDT_NO_CALLBACKS
	help
	  Enable a watchdog driver backed by Xen SCHEDOP_watchdog.

	  This driver exposes Xen domain watchdog timers through Zephyr's
	  watchdog API for the current Xen domain. Xen provides two domain
	  watchdog timer slots, exposed as configurable Zephyr watchdog
	  channels.
	  Expiration is handled by Xen according to the domain's on_watchdog
	  policy, so pre-timeout callbacks are not supported.
	  Xen accepts watchdog timeouts in whole seconds. Timeout windows shorter
	  than one second are rejected, and longer millisecond values are rounded
	  up to the next second.
